* Board 1: oscillator 1's waveshapers (Fig. 9-3; service manual 2.16), as drawn, from the
* sawtooth on Q3's collector on (+4 V at the start of the cycle, falling to -4 V, then the
* reset). saw: Q3's collector; width: the RECTANGULAR WIDTH bias from the WAVEFORM switch
* (pin 22B); sawo, tri, rect: the SAWTOOTH, TRIANGLE and RECTANGULAR outputs.
.subckt shapers saw width sawo tri rect vp vn
* sawtooth output divider
r34 saw sawo 4.3k
r33 sawo 0 4.7k
* triangle: Q2 saturates while the sawtooth is positive (its collector follows it) and
* inverts once it is negative; follower Q1
q2 n saw e2 Q2N3392
r29 e2 vn 10k
r3 vp n 10.7k
r14 n vn 150k
q1 vp n e1 Q2N3392
r28 e1 tri 750
r23 tri vn 8.2k
* rectangle: Schmitt trigger Q11 / Q12 on the sawtooth and the width bias
r40 saw b 43k
r1 width b 43k
r44 b vn 390k
r2 b rc 910k
q11 c11 b 0 Q2N4058
r39 c11 b12 100k
r35 b12 vn 100k
q12 rc b12 vn Q2N3392
r13 rc rect 6.2k
r22 rect 0 4.7k
.ends
